	(text "Buzzer: magnetic, drive with a 2.7 kHz square wave (LEDC PWM).\nR39 keeps Q3 off while the ESP32 boots."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 205.74 149.86 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "0491c0d2-e0e1-48cf-b598-d6a730f80ba3")
	)
	(text "Servo headers J9/J10: GND, VSERVO (battery voltage 4.0-6.4 V, 2 A eFuse), PWM (servo plug: brown/black, red, orange/white).\nUART J11 (lidar etc.): GND, +5 V, RX (= device TX), TX (= device RX). Logic is 3.3 V only.\n+5V_EXT (lidar) is current-limited to 0.83 A. Use servos rated for 6 V (SG90, MG90S ...)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 139.7 25.4 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "56782a89-fd11-4142-a312-11c80fdf16c3")
	)
	(text "Signal protection: 1 k in series with every servo, UART and GPIO signal, between the header and the ESP32.\nA stray 5-6 V wire is limited to a few mA. Side effect: J12 pins can source or sink only about 1-2 mA, so drive bigger loads through a transistor."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 157.48 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "a40df641-d826-43c4-a3fd-0e865cc8daf1")
	)
	(text "I2C: J7 = Qwiic / STEMMA QT socket (JST SH 1.0 mm), J8 = 1x4 male header for Dupont wires.\nBoth use the Qwiic pin order (GND, 3.3 V, SDA, SCL), 4.7k pull-ups to 3.3 V.\nSensor power comes from +3V3_EXT (current-limited to 0.57 A)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 25.4 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "a8c17bae-b9d1-4476-9a22-9d2bd170487f")
	)
	(text "RGB LED D3 runs from +5V through D4 (about 4.3 V),\nso 3.3 V data is a valid high (VIH = 0.7 x VDD)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 127 149.86 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
